"""THE WORLD - Tuesday 24 November 2026.

One page, one day: a newspaper front page summing up 23 stories from six
continents in a single 1024x1024 image - a lead on Nvidia's whiplash day,
twelve story cards, a dotted world map with one big marker per story, a
by-the-numbers rail led by the $233bn Nvidia wipeout, nine world briefs,
and the day's sport.

Pure Python standard library: no dependencies, no network, fully
deterministic (same bytes on every run). The PNG is written into the
directory named by MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR, or into the current directory
when that variable is not set.
"""
